## A Habit Worth Building Early

```bash
rm file.txt
```
Deletes instantly, permanently, with zero confirmation. No Recycle Bin to fall back on.

```bash
rm -i file.txt
```
Asks for confirmation first — a small habit that can save you from a mistake you can't undo.

**Takeaway:** If you're new to the Linux command line, get comfortable using `-i` before you get comfortable using `rm` on its own. It's much easier to build the safe habit early than to learn it the hard way.

